				"bounds": {
					"height": 30,
					"width": 195,
					"x": 129.52178955078125,
					"y": 327.2474365234375
				},
				"class": {
					"id": "77697265-AEE3-4B9D-BBD5-6Ae4CCD5aB30",
					"version": 1
				},
				"clock": "video",
				"color": "ffff6a00",
				"constants": {
					"input0": {
						"type": "float",
						"value": 0
					}
				},
				"hidden": [
					"flow",
					"input0-type",
					"input0-dimensions"
				],
				"name": "Mix > 1-x *25"
			},
			"126": {
				"attributes": {
					"alignment": {
						"type": "integer",
						"value": 0
					},
					"fill": {
						"type": "bool",
						"value": true
					},
					"font-size": {
						"type": "float",
						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "DigiGl!tch\n\nThis patch demonstrates the DigiGl!tch blend mode. This blend mode blends in the new signal in distorted blocky bits. As the mix parameter is turned up, more blocks show up, creating the final image and completing the transition.\n\nThis effect is really customizable, we made this tutorial so that you can make your own \"partial\"-mixer. The concept is rather simple: construct a mask that can morph from nothing to a full white image."
					}
				},
				"bounds": {
					"height": 199.6346893310546875,
					"width": 682.5435791015625,
					"x": -1419.750244140625,
					"y": -741.47418212890625
				},
				"class": {
					"id": "77697265-3C1D-467D-A722-0FC566538374",
					"version": 1
				},
				"clock": "video",
				"color": "ffd0c117",
				"constants": {},
				"hidden": [
					"text",
					"alignment",
					"font-size",
					"fill"
				],
				"name": "Comment"
			},
			"127": {
				"attributes": {
					"alignment": {
						"type": "integer",
						"value": 0
					},
					"fill": {
						"type": "bool",
						"value": false
					},
					"font-size": {
						"type": "float",
						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "MIX\n\nThe Mix parameter is the only float in the patch and will be the parameter animated by the video opacity slider in Arena and Avenue.\n\nAt 0 we don't want any image and at 1 we want a completely white image to use as a mask.\nIn between we want a partially white image to use as a mask. \n\nThe 1-x node is used to flip the 0 to 1 range to a 1 to 0 range."
					}
				},
				"bounds": {
					"height": 360.26983642578125,
					"width": 656.424072265625,
					"x": -1419.560791015625,
					"y": -483.197357177734375
				},
				"class": {
					"id": "77697265-3C1D-467D-A722-0FC566538374",
					"version": 1
				},
				"clock": "video",
				"color": "ffff6a00",
				"constants": {},
				"hidden": [
					"text",
					"alignment",
					"font-size",
					"fill"
				],
				"name": "Comment"
			},
			"129": {
				"attributes": {
					"alignment": {
						"type": "integer",
						"value": 0
					},
					"fill": {
						"type": "bool",
						"value": false
					},
					"font-size": {
						"type": "float",
						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "BIG BLOCKS\n\nThe big blocks are a grid of 25 Rectangles pushed into position using the Grid Pattern node using the Transform node and rendered to texture using a Shape Render.\n\nThe value coming from the Mix parameter runs from 1 to 0 (due to the 1-x node).\nWe multiply this by 25, this creates a range running from 25 to 0 coming from the Multiply node.\nNext we create a Sequence running from 1 to 25 and check if the Mix is Less than the Sequence\nBy doing this we end up with a collection of booleans (true or false).\nAt a mix of 0 the entire collection is false, at a mix of 1 the entire collection is true.\n\nWe Shuffle this collection for a more random look before applying the booleans to the scale of the rectangles.\nTrue will be interpreted as 1 and False will be interpreted as 0, so technically  speaking, the shapes are always there, just infinitely small.\nThis little trick allows us to make the rectangles appear and disappear as the Mix slider moves."
					}
				},
				"bounds": {
					"height": 733.77911376953125,
					"width": 1348.5916748046875,
					"x": -695.96002197265625,
					"y": -483.68927001953125
				},
				"class": {
					"id": "77697265-3C1D-467D-A722-0FC566538374",
					"version": 1
				},
				"clock": "video",
				"color": "fff26eb5",
				"constants": {},
				"hidden": [
					"text",
					"alignment",
					"font-size",
					"fill"
				],
				"name": "Comment"
			},
