			"130": {
				"attributes": {
					"flow": {
						"type": "flow",
						"value": "signal"
					},
					"input0-dimensions": {
						"type": "integer",
						"value": 1
					},
					"input0-type": {
						"type": "type",
						"value": "texture2d"
					}
				},
				"bounds": {
					"height": 30,
					"width": 195,
					"x": 1090.7626953125,
					"y": 346.696014404296875
				},
				"class": {
					"id": "77697265-AEE3-4B9D-BBD5-6Ae4CCD5aB30",
					"version": 1
				},
				"clock": "video",
				"color": "ffae7bff",
				"constants": {
					"input0": {
						"type": "texture2d",
						"value": null
					}
				},
				"hidden": [
					"flow",
					"input0-type",
					"input0-dimensions"
				],
				"name": "The Noise"
			},
			"131": {
				"attributes": {
					"alignment": {
						"type": "integer",
						"value": 0
					},
					"fill": {
						"type": "bool",
						"value": false
					},
					"font-size": {
						"type": "float",
						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "THE NOISE\n\nAlthough there is a lot going on down here, everything is rather simple in nature.\nWe've got 3 static nodes that generate the basis of our noise.\nNote that the textures of the Static nodes are at 1\/8th of the patch size to save processing power.\n\nThe count outlet of the Metronome is multiplied by arbitrary values to generate 3 distinct static patterns to avoid repetition\/recognizability.\nNext the static textures are treated with the Pixelate effect to create even thicker and more lo-fi textures at three different resolutions.\nThis increases the randomness and due to the different pixelate resolutions we get blobby pixels after we Add and Subtract the textures later on.\n\nNote that the original Mix parameter is here as well (running 0 to 1).\nThis is multiplied with a float called Resolution (which you can change if you like!)\nAfter the multiplication we send these values to the columns and rows parameters of the Pixelate nodes.\n\nAs the mix value goes up, so does the resolution of the noise.\nWhen all is said and done we subtract two static nodes from each other and add the third.\nThere isn't really a science behind this, you can mix and match the statics as you like until you get something that looks cool"
					}
				},
				"bounds": {
					"height": 1187.6427001953125,
					"width": 1947.7574462890625,
					"x": -1067.4517822265625,
					"y": 393.661224365234375
				},
				"class": {
					"id": "77697265-3C1D-467D-A722-0FC566538374",
					"version": 1
				},
				"clock": "video",
				"color": "ff20c7bb",
				"constants": {},
				"hidden": [
					"text",
					"alignment",
					"font-size",
					"fill"
				],
				"name": "Comment"
			},
			"139": {
				"attributes": {
					"alignment": {
						"type": "integer",
						"value": 0
					},
					"fill": {
						"type": "bool",
						"value": false
					},
					"font-size": {
						"type": "float",
						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "NOISE GATE\n\nHere we check if the Mix (running from 25 to 0) is greater than 1.\nIf that is the case we want the static noise to be used.\n\nIf we don't do this we would have the noise acting up at when the video opacity is at 1.\nThis would suck as we would never have a proper transition from clip to clip.\n\nThis is also where we resize our 1\/8 sized texture to be at the patch resolution.\nNote that the sampling method of the Resize node is changed to \"Nearest\" to maintain a crisp image."
					}
				},
				"bounds": {
					"height": 396.718841552734375,
					"width": 748.96539306640625,
					"x": 1076.126220703125,
					"y": 20.82060623168945312
				},
				"class": {
					"id": "77697265-3C1D-467D-A722-0FC566538374",
					"version": 1
				},
				"clock": "video",
				"color": "ffae7bff",
				"constants": {},
				"hidden": [
					"text",
					"alignment",
					"font-size",
					"fill"
				],
				"name": "Comment"
			},
			"14": {
				"attributes": {
					"flow": {
						"type": "flow",
						"value": "signal"
					},
					"has-max": {
						"type": "bool",
						"value": true
